08515, 123.28064457208207, 398.24185162755975, 138.41723318778037]}, {"r0": 0, "r1": 0, "c0": 3, "c1": 3, "text": "Weed pollen", "bbox": [408.1401463458044, 119.70127118107844, 506.56247931091883, 133.95688558830736]}, {"r0": 0, "r1": 0, "c0": 4, "c1": 4, "text": "Mould spores", "bbox": [515.451691692574, 115.14635172714107, 644.4055262357599, 130.4108565615506]}, {"r0": 1, "r1": 1, "c0": 0, "c1": 0, "text": "British Columbia (Coastal)", "bbox": [57.903051033744255, 149.17112397217403, 101.67146744855557, 216.1719338524844]}, {"r0": 1, "r1": 1, "c0": 1, "c1": 1, "text": "• Season: early February to mid-July • Primarily deciduous trees (alder, birch, poplar, elm, oak)", "bbox": [108.40812533249925, 143.72304440783938, 266.5437323988583, 214.50303178902823]}, {"r0": 1, "r1": 1, "c0": 2, "c1": 2, "text": "• Season: end of April to September • Highest grass concentrations: early June to mid-July", "bbox": [273.6878642980447, 139.29411642062016, 400.5739681786091, 209.04148755338508]}, {"r0": 1, "r1": 1, "c0": 3, "c1": 3, "text": "• Not usually a major factor; no native ragweed", "bbox": [408.6689346929976, 135.71474302961656, 508.8945958619683, 204.58113995391207]}, {"r0": 1, "r1": 1, "c0": 4, "c1": 4, "text": "• Levels higher in the spring; increase further in September and October • Most prevalent spores: Cladosporium and basidiomycetes", "bbox": [515.9804800397671, 131.15982357567918, 646.7376427868094, 201.0351109271553]}, {"r0": 2, "r1": 2, "c0": 0, "c1": 0, "text": "British Columbia (Interior)", "bbox": [60.5976280401642, 230.77188780341592, 103.645610120571, 275.9555472227838]}, {"r0": 2, "r1": 2, "c0": 1, "c1": 1, "text": "• Season: late March to mid-July • Primarily deciduous trees (willow, birch, poplar)", "bbox": [111.10270233891919, 225.32380823908127, 268.51787507087374, 274.2866451593277]}, {"r0": 2, "r1": 2, "c0": 2, "c1": 2, "text": "• Season starts in early May in southern parts of the province; starts up to 1 month later in northern parts", "bbox": [276.38244130446463, 220.89488025186205, 402.54811085062454, 268.82510092368454]}, {"r0": 2, "r1": 2, "c0": 3, "c1": 3, "text": "• Ragweed is minimal", "bbox": [411.36351169941753, 217.31550686085845, 510.86873853398373, 264.3647533242115]}, {"r0": 2, "r1": 2, "c0": 4, "c1": 4, "text": "• Cladosporium can occur from April to late fall", "bbox": [518.675057046187, 212.76058740692108, 648.7117854588248, 260.81872429745476]}, {"r0": 3, "r1": 3, "c0": 0, "c1": 0, "text": "Prairies", "bbox": [62.211553698364604, 279.64693058832, 105.61782870323376, 335.68089276088347]}, {"r0": 3, "r1": 3, "c0": 1, "c1": 1, "text": "• Season starts in the first week of April and continues through June&#8226 Main deciduous trees: birch and poplar; alder, maple, elm, oak, ash, and willow may also contribute", "bbox": [112.71662799711962, 274.19885102398536, 270.4900936535365, 334.01199069742734]}, {"r0": 3, "r1": 3, "c0": 2, "c1": 2, "text": "• Season starts in mid‐May and continues to the end of September&#8226 Peak season is usually mid‐June to early July", "bbox": [277.99636696266504, 269.7699230367661, 404.5203294332873, 328.5504464617842]}, {"r0": 3, "r1": 3, "c0": 3, "c1": 3, "text": "• Most common weeds: nettles or sage brush&#8226 Some ragweed, especially in Manitoba)", "bbox": [412.97743735761793, 266.19054964576253, 512.8409571166465, 324.09009886231115]}, {"r0": 3, "r1": 3, "c0": 4, "c1": 4, "text": "• Can occur through the spring, summer, and early fall&#8226 Alternaria and Cladosporium are the predominant moulds", "bbox": [520.2889827043874, 261.63563019182516, 650.6840040414875, 320.54406983555435]}, {"r0": 4, "r1": 4, "c0": 0, "c1": 0, "text": "Ontario and Quebec", "bbox": [64.18409132645573, 339.38193788430993, 110.11605265216383, 471.9020915769304]}, {"r0": 4, "r1": 4, "c0": 1, "c1": 1, "text": "• Season starts early April in southern Ontario and Quebec; may occur 6 weeks later in northern areas • In southern Ontario, most common are deciduous trees (birch, poplar, oak, maple, ash, elm, mulberry, willow, chestnut, hickory) • In northern Ontario, birch and poplar most common • In Quebec, ash, poplar, birch most common; maple, alder and oak are less prevalent", "bbox": [114.68916562521073, 333.9338583199753, 274.98831760246657, 470.23318951347426]}, {"r0": 4, "r1": 4, "c0": 2, "c1": 2, "text": "• Season starts mid-to-late May; a couple of weeks later in northern areas • Latter part of May and mid- June are peak seasons for grass pollination", "bbox": [279.96890459075615, 329.50493033275603, 409.01855338221736, 464.7716452778311]}, {"r0": 4, "r1": 4, "c0": 3, "c1": 3, "text": "• Ragweed season in Southern Ontario and Southwestern Quebec begins early-to-mid August • Reaches peak in late August/early September • Stops at first frost • Nettle and plantain can also contribute", "bbox": [414.94997498570905, 325.92555694175246, 517.3391810655766, 460.3112976783581]}, {"r0": 4, "r1": 4, "c0": 4, "c1": 4, "text": "• Occur during spring, summer and fall months • Concentrations may be higher late summer to fall months in Quebec • Alternaria and Cladosporium are the predominant moulds", "bbox": [522.2615203324785, 321.3706374878151, 655.1822279904176, 456.76526865160133]}, {"r0": 5, "r1": 5, "c0": 0, "c1": 0, "text": "Maritimes", "bbox": [68.68295091204698, 475.6223858949229, 111.72679767286283, 520.6808140677902]}, {"r0": 5, "r1": 5, "c0": 1, "c1": 1, "text": "• Season in New Brunswick and Nova Scotia: late March to last week of June • Primarily deciduous trees (birch, poplar, alder, maple, oak, and ash)", "bbox": [119.18802521080195, 470.1743063305882, 276.5990626231656, 519.0119120043339]}, {"r0": 5, "r1": 5, "c0": 2, "c1": 2, "text": "• Season: mid-May to end of September • Peaks in early June", "bbox": [284.46776417634743, 465.745378343369, 410.6292984029164, 513.5503677686908]}, {"r0": 5, "r1": 5, "c0": 3, "c1": 3, "text": "• Ragweed: early August to end of September", "bbox": [419.4488345713003, 462.16600495236537, 518.9499260862756, 509.0900201692177]}, {"r0": 5, "r1": 5, "c0": 4, "c1": 4, "text": "• Levels higher during the late summer and early fall months • Alternaria and Cladosporium are the predominant moulds", "bbox": [526.7603799180698, 457.611085498428, 656.7929730111166, 505.543991142461]}]}]}}, "seconds_all_modes": 0.6668687080964446, "estimated_angle": 1.6846843178962914}